      "content": "That's pretty intense. It sounds like people treated them almost like a real pest problem, like dealing with rats or insects. \n\nI'm curious about the documentation, though. Since these \"Sand-Whisperers\" and \"Crag-Rascals\" were so well-known, were there actually any historical records or travel journals from that era that mention them specifically by those names? Or is this mostly just stuff passed down through oral tradition?",
